ose guarantees, actual compaction or recovery loss."],"unknowns":["Whether the applicable contract requires Persist to propagate every sink completion error.","Whether repeated Close after failed Close has an independently supported success meaning beyond a tolerated repeated resource operation.","Whether a contract-compliant Persist can return nil after incomplete publication, including prior failed Close or cancellation.","Whether fresh-success publication expectations apply to repeated completion after failure.","Which application Persist implementation and snapshot adapter are selected in an actual deployment.","Whether repository cluster construction connects the tested callback and file adapter to actual Raft snapshot orchestration.","What the public snapshot API promises when its completion future succeeds and whether that expectation applies independently of callback contract compliance.","Which publication guarantees apply under noSync and operating-system variants; crash durability remains unestablished.","Whether the controlled pre-publication failure is reachable within the parent's applicable legal history and fault contract.","Whether any completion mismatch causes actual log reclamation or loss of recovery evidence.","How concurrent retention or later removal affects availability beyond the child's immediate observation."],"priority":1,"trigger_rationale":"The supplied child result resolves the bounded question of MockSnapshot.Persist reporting success despite an observed pre-publication failure and unavailable snapshot ID. The attached source separately shows takeSnapshot calling Close again and runSnapshots installing an opener after takeSnapshot succeeds. This supports continuing the parent, but does not promote the child result to an orchestration or recovery violation. The next reads target actual repository wiring and the public completion expectation; they can distinguish a separately checkable consumer responsibility from a path whose applicability still depends on an unsupported callback assumption."},"source_receipt":{"id":"5dc84f0f98f24a99a5c8edce3c2041b0","snapshot_id":"47affc6f0769463ca2bf93f250308d6c","purpose":"depth","status":"complete","items":[{"request":{"file":"testing.go","start_line":261,"end_line":550,"reason":"Inspect repository cluster construction following the acquired cluster declaration. Determine whether and how MockFSM, FileSnapshotStore and real Raft instances are connected, and identify an existing execution context for the child result without assuming production deployment or legal fault reachability."},"status":"acquired","material_ids":["testing.go:261:550"],"new_chars":8917,"new_chunks":0,"reason":"","file_metadata":{"file":"testing.go","lines":874,"content_digest":"426e32dca108d637c6f718a27cb5405b93a507a8f1247249fba90e23eabdfe23","snapshot_id":"47affc6f0769463ca2bf93f250308d6c","encoding":"utf-8"}},{"request":{"file":"api.go","start_line":950,"end_line":1150,"reason":"Locate the public snapshot request and completion contract and its connection to runSnapshots. Determine whether caller-visible success supplies a separately attributable expectation for publication. If the relevant declaration is outside this range, return its location for a focused follow-up."},"status":"acquired","material_ids":["api.go:950:1150"],"new_chars":6961,"new_chunks":1,"reason":"","file_metadata":{"file":"api.go","lines":1282,"content_digest":"499a72c01096912e85d16381f4640ac6d29f8c2b91cabbdae8530bdcbeb89a4a","snapshot_id":"47affc6f0769463ca2bf93f250308d6c","encoding":"utf-8"}}],"partial_policy":"independent_ranges_with_explicit_defer","related_ids":["F_file_snapshot_fresh_close","B_file_sink_close","B_take_snapshot"],"reason":"When takeSnapshot consumes a successful FileSnapshotSink.Close result, do the applicable sink and FSMSnapshot.Persist contracts ensure that the snapshot has completed the publication steps needed before snapshot metadata advances and logs are compacted, including legally rea